====================================================================================================
1. Anthropic 3-SAT decision machine (rates/PaddedDescent): explicit floor, TM degree q
====================================================================================================
sOf n = floor(3(floor(log2 floor(log2 n)) - 911)/19);  exhaustive while s < s0K 3 = 128;  pad 2^{2^131 (n/2^s + 1)}
  q =     1 : rate q*2^(131-s) < 1 needs s >= 132  <=>  floor(log2 log2 n) >= 1747  i.e. n >= 2^(2^1747)
  q =     2 : rate q*2^(131-s) < 1 needs s >= 133  <=>  floor(log2 log2 n) >= 1754  i.e. n >= 2^(2^1754)
  q =    10 : rate q*2^(131-s) < 1 needs s >= 136  <=>  floor(log2 log2 n) >= 1773  i.e. n >= 2^(2^1773)
  q =  1000 : rate q*2^(131-s) < 1 needs s >= 142  <=>  floor(log2 log2 n) >= 1811  i.e. n >= 2^(2^1811)
  (exhaustive search for all n < 2^(2^1722); ThreeSatRateStatement.lean says 2^(2^518), a weaker, true bound)

====================================================================================================
2. Anthropic #3-SAT, m-route (Theorem 1 in m), k = 3, m = alpha*n
====================================================================================================
rate = needTop/n, needTop = max(search 3K^8 size K, P(2g/K+1), (K-1)lam, solver); T <= q(|x|+2^needTop+1)^q

