====================================================================================================
6. OpenAI Engine II (thm:tensor-contraction): explicit parameter threshold only
====================================================================================================
u_d = floor(eps*lam/2^d), eps = 2^-17, depth d < (log2 C + log2 lam / 2)/3; bound lam^(4/5) <= u_d at the deepest
active call needs eps*lam^(5/6)/C^(1/3) >= lam^(4/5)  <=>  lam >= 2^510 * C^10 (C = wire density constant, >= 1).
At d = 0 alone: lam >= eps^-5 = 2^85.  So Engine II as written applies only for log2(wires) >= 2^85 (d=0) / 2^510 (all depths).
Its rate also has the explicit leaf term H/n = wires/(n*floor(sqrt(lam))) >= 1/sqrt(lam); all other constants are O_C(.).
